# nightshift's runtime output. Everything else it writes is committed on purpose —
# the manifest, the gates, the board, the corrections log and the install receipt are
# all properties of the repo. These four are not.
#
# Comments live on their own line: a `#` after a pattern is part of the pattern.

# Per-run worker logs and transcripts. Large, and meaningful only on the machine
# that produced them.
.ai/runs/

# The preflight receipt. Names a commit SHA on one machine; a committed one would
# unblock a push somebody else never checked.
.ai/.preflight

# Per-machine dispatch config, resolved from the committed .ai/hosts.json.
.ai/host.json

# The stop file. Its presence halts the runner, so it must never arrive by pull.
.ai/STOP

# Obsidian's window state: which panes are open, which tab is active, where each
# one is scrolled. Rewritten on almost every interaction, including just looking at
# the board -- so a tracked one is dirty again seconds after you commit it, and the
# runner refuses to dispatch on a dirty tree. That is the whole failure: opening the
# board to read it is what stops the board being worked.
#
# Deliberately NOT `.obsidian/` wholesale. `init` writes community-plugins.json and
# core-plugins.json, and those are real shared config -- ignoring the directory would
# mean every machine re-does the plugin setup by hand, which is the thing wiring them
# was for. Only the volatile files are named.
.obsidian/workspace.json
.obsidian/workspace-mobile.json
